<article class="env-definition" id="023W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/023W">Definition <span data-tag="023W">35.34.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\{ X_ i \to S\} _{i \in I}$ be a family of morphisms with target $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>descent datum $(V_ i, \varphi _{ij})$ relative to the family $\{ X_ i \to S\} $</em> is given by a scheme $V_ i$ over $X_ i$ for each $i \in I$, an isomorphism $\varphi _{ij} : V_ i \times _ S X_ j \to X_ i \times _ S V_ j$ of schemes over $X_ i \times _ S X_ j$ for each pair $(i, j) \in I^2$ such that for every triple of indices $(i, j, k) \in I^3$ the diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ V_ i \times _ S X_ j \times _ S X_ k \ar[rd]^{\text{pr}_{01}^*\varphi _{ij}} \ar[rr]_{\text{pr}_{02}^*\varphi _{ik}} &  &  X_ i \times _ S X_ j \times _ S V_ k\\  &  X_ i \times _ S V_ j \times _ S X_ k \ar[ru]^{\text{pr}_{12}^*\varphi _{jk}} }  \]
</div>
<p>
 of schemes over $X_ i \times _ S X_ j \times _ S X_ k$ commutes (with obvious notation). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>morphism $\psi : (V_ i, \varphi _{ij}) \to (V'_ i, \varphi '_{ij})$ of descent data</em> is given by a family $\psi = (\psi _ i)_{i \in I}$ of morphisms of $X_ i$-schemes $\psi _ i : V_ i \to V'_ i$ such that all the diagrams 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ V_ i \times _ S X_ j \ar[r]_{\varphi _{ij}} \ar[d]_{\psi _ i \times \text{id}} &  X_ i \times _ S V_ j \ar[d]^{\text{id} \times \psi _ j} \\  V'_ i \times _ S X_ j \ar[r]^{\varphi '_{ij}} &  X_ i \times _ S V'_ j }  \]
</div>
<p>
 commute. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>